    <!-- Dialogs -->
    <string name="dialog_dns_help">DNS injected when VPN starts (addDnsServer); empty = default.\nDomestic DNS recommended (default 223.5.5.5 / 2400:3200::1):\nthe engine queries it directly and anti-pollution-checks the\nreply (domestic DNS is the one that can return poisoned answers);\nforeign domains fall back to foreign DNS via the proxy.\nA foreign DNS also works, but every query then rides the\nupstream proxy, which must support UDP.\nRestart VPN to apply.</string>
    <string name="toast_invalid_dns">Invalid DNS address format</string>
    <string name="dialog_exclude_title">Excluded routes (API 33+)</string>
    <string name="dialog_exclude_hint">One CIDR per line, e.g. 192.168.1.0/24</string>
    <string name="dialog_exclude_help">These networks bypass the VPN tunnel (split tunnel); restart VPN to apply.</string>
    <string name="cd_choose_service_mode">Choose service mode</string>
    <string name="dialog_service_help">VPN tunnel: takes over system traffic for smart routing (default).\nProxy only: no VPN mode; runs the engine\'s SOCKS5 proxy (:1080, LAN-accessible).\nSwitching while running auto-restarts.</string>

